<!doctype html>
<html>
	<head>
		{{render "_head" $}}
		<title>{{tr "titleprefix"}}{{tr "subsonic_title"}}</title>
		<style>
			main p {
				padding-left: 1em;
			}
			#help:target {
				background: var(--hi-bg);
			}
            main h3, main img {
                margin-left: 1em;
                margin-top: 1em;
            }
            table caption {
                font-weight: bold;
            }
            table {
                width: 100%;
                table-layout: fixed;
                max-width: min(36em, 98vw);
            }
            table, td {
                border: 1px solid var(--fg, black);
                overflow: wrap;
                overflow-wrap: break-word;
            }
            td {
                padding: 1ch;
            }
            table td:nth-child(1) {
                text-decoration: underline;
            }
            table td:nth-child(2) {
            }
            main img {
                 max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
                 max-height:100vh;
            }
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		{{render "_nav" $}}
		<main>
			<h2>{{tr "subsonic_title"}}</h2>

            <p>{{tr "subsonic_intro" (tr "service_name")}}</p>

            <ol>
                 <li>
                    <a href="#basic" class="navlink">{{tr "subsonic_basic"}}</a>
                    <ol>
                        <li><a href="#auth" class="navlink">{{tr "subsonic_auth"}}</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#support" class="navlink">{{tr "subsonic_support"}}</a></li>
                    </ol>
                 </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="#ios" class="navlink">iOS</a>
                    <ol>
                        <li><a href="#amperfy" class="navlink">Amperfy</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#playsub" class="navlink">play:Sub</a></li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="#android" class="navlink">Android</a>
                    <ol>
                        <li><a href="#tempus" class="navlink">Tempus</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#symfonium" class="navlink">Symfonium</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#subtracks" class="navlink">Subtracks</a></li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="#other" class="navlink">Others</a>
                </li>
            </ol>

            <h2 id="basic">Basic settings</h2>
            <section>
                <table>
                    <caption>{{tr "subsonic_settings"}}</caption>
                    <tr>
                        <td>{{tr "serveraddr"}}</td>
                        <td><code>https://{{domain}}</code></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>{{tr "username"}}</td>
                        <td>
                            {{with $.User.Email}}
                                <code>{{.}}</code>
                            {{else}}
                                (Your e-mail address)
                            {{end}}
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>{{tr "password"}}</td>
                        <td>
                            An app password from <a href="/settings#apps">settings</a>, not your account password
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>{{tr "subsonic_authsetting"}}</td>
                        <td>
                            Plain-text password mode or API key login for strict app passwords; the default token method works with compatibility ones
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

                <h3 id="auth">{{tr "subsonic_auth"}}</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Music apps log in with an app password, never your account password. Create one per device in <a href="/settings#apps">settings</a> and revoke it there if the device is lost.</li>
                    <li>App passwords only work for music apps. They cannot sign in to this site or change account settings.</li>
                    <li>App passwords are <b>strict</b> by default: your library can only be unlocked while that device is connected. Enable plain-text password or API key mode in your app settings. If your app lacks support, use a <b>compatibility</b> app password instead.</li>
                    <li>Always connect over HTTPS. Some apps transmit credentials in the URL query string.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3 id="support">{{tr "subsonic_support"}}</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>[x] Basic browsing and playback</li>
                    <li>[x] Album art</li>
                    <li>[x] Search</li>
                    <li>[x] Sorting by recent, newest, etc.</li>
                    <li>[x] Starring (favorites)</li>
                    <li>[x] Proper pagination</li>
                    <li>[x] Playlists</li>
                    <li>[ ] Bookmarks (planned)</li>
                    <li>[ ] Chat</li>
                    <li>[ ] Podcasts</li>
                    <li>[ ] Similar artists</li>
                    <li>[x] Lyrics</li>
                    <li>[ ] Last.fm scrobbling (planned)</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <h2 id="ios">iOS</h2>

            <h3 id="amperfy">Amperfy</h3>
            <p>Password: a <b>compatibility</b> app password. Amperfy signs in with the default token method, which strict passwords don't allow.</p>
            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Open Amperfy and choose Subsonic as the server type.</li>
                    <li>Fill in the server address, username and a compatibility app password as above.</li>
                </ol>
            </p>

            <h3 id="playsub">play:Sub</h3>
            <p>Download: <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/play-sub-music-streamer/id955329386" target="_blank" class="navlink">App Store</a></p>
            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Tap the "play:Sub" menu icon on the bottom right.</li>
                    <li>Tap the name of the server in the first menu item.</li>
                    <li>Tap "Selected server"</li>
                    <li>Tap "Add server"</li>
                    <li>Fill in the server address, server name, username and app password as above, and turn on plain-text password if offered.</li>
                </ol>
            </p>

            <br>

            <h2 id="android">Android</h2>

            <h3 id="tempus">Tempus</h3>
            <p>Password: a <b>strict</b> app password. Tempus can sign in with an OpenSubsonic API key or a plain-text password, both of which strict passwords allow.</p>
            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Add a server and fill in the server address, username and app password as above.</li>
                    <li>Turn on API key login or the plain-text password option if your version offers it.</li>
                </ol>
            </p>

            <h3 id="symfonium">Symfonium</h3>
            <p>Download: <a href="https://symfonium.app" target="_blank" class="navlink">symfonium.app</a></p>
            <p>Password: a <b>strict</b> app password if you turn on its plain-text (legacy) password option in the server settings; otherwise use a <b>compatibility</b> one.</p>
            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Add a Subsonic or OpenSubsonic media provider.</li>
                    <li>Fill in the server address, username and app password as above.</li>
                </ol>
            </p>

            <h3 id="subtracks">Subtracks</h3>
            <p>Download: <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.subtracks&hl=en&gl=US&pli=1" target="_blank" class="navlink">Google Play</a></p>
            <p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Tap the Settings icon on the bottom right</li>
                    <li>Tap Add server</li>
                    <li>Fill in the server address, username and app password as above.</li>
                    <li>Enable "force plain text password".</li>
                </ol>
            </p>

            <h2 id="other">Others</h2>

            <p>Most apps that support Subsonic or OpenSubsonic should work. You can find more at <a href="https://www.navidrome.org/apps/">the Navidrome apps page</a> for many other devices.</p>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>